rf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 7 grids in Hampton County runs from 1951 to 2025, and October to November came in under 90% of normal in 42 of those 75 years. In 2025, November to December finished at 44% of normal and January to February at 46% on the middle of the grids. So far in 2026, March to April came in at 14% of normal on the middle of the grids. Every grid had its driest year in 1954, with grids 15197 and 15796 at 63%.</p>"}
